3690 kṣīṇá 'worn away' ŚBr., 'feeble' Mn. [~ * jhīna-. — √kṣi ²] Pa. khīṇa - 'destroyed, exhausted'; Pk. khīṇa -, chī° 'destroyed, tired, weak, thin'; Gy. eur. khino 'tired';
Dm. c̣hin (< * kṣiṇṇa - NTS xii 165, see below) 'darkness < *waning (of moon)' NOPhal 32; Tir. čīne 'old';
Sh. pales. čĩṛo 'black'; Bshk. (Biddulph) čün 'dark' ( c̣h ?); Phal. c̣hiṇ 'darkness' AO xviii 230; S. khīṇu 'emaciated'; Ku. khiṇīṇo 'to be used up'; A. khīniba 'to grow thin'; B. khin 'emaciated'; Or. khīna 'thin, weak' (< * kṣiṇṇa -); Mth. chīn 'slender, lean';
Bhoj. khīn 'emaciated'; OAw. khīna 'thin, tiny'; H. khīn 'worn away', khinnā 'to be worn away', chīn 'wasted,
thin'; OG. khīṇa 'exhausted'; M. śīṇ m. 'weariness', śiṇṇẽ 'to be weary' (LM 423 < śīrṇá -). kṣaiṇya-; *kṣīṇakūṭin-, kṣīṇāsrava-, kṣīṇōpāya -. Addenda: kṣīṇá-: A. chinā (phonet. s -) 'small, thin'.
